Upstream-Status: Not-applicable
Exit: Drop if freedesktop-sdk's base FFmpeg enables all native codecs.
Subject: ffmpeg: enable all native encoders and decoders

Replace Fedora's allowlist so the host FFmpeg handles H.264, HEVC, VC-1
and VVC, including through its VA-API and Vulkan hwaccels. No external
codec libraries are added, so FFmpeg stays LGPL.

Resolves: projectbluefin/dakota#1686

diff --git a/elements/components/ffmpeg.bst b/elements/components/ffmpeg.bst
--- a/elements/components/ffmpeg.bst
+++ b/elements/components/ffmpeg.bst
@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@
 # SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
 
 kind: make
-description: Base ffmpeg we ship in the SDK, no patented codecs
+description: Base ffmpeg we ship in the SDK
 
 (@):
 - elements/include/ffmpeg.yml
@@ -118,6 +118,5 @@ variables:
     zero12v,zerocodec,zlib,zmbv,%{extra-decoders}
 
   conf-extra: >-
-    --enable-encoder=%{encoders}
-    --enable-decoder=%{decoders}
-    --disable-decoder="h264,hevc,vc1,vvc"
+    --enable-encoders
+    --enable-decoders
